":[43,74],"##The Three Use Cases That Pay for the Learning Curve":[75,80],"##The Three Use Cases That Pay for the Learning Curve#{1}":[77,80],"##1\\. Measure validation — the auditor’s power tool":[81,102],"##1\\. Measure validation — the auditor’s power tool#{1}":[83,102],"##2\\. Relationship and data-quality validation":[103,108],"##2\\. Relationship and data-quality validation#{1}":[105,108],"##3\\. Living documentation":[109,112],"##3\\. Living documentation#{1}":[111,112],"##A Worked Example: The Reconciliation Notebook":[113,174],"##A Worked Example: The Reconciliation Notebook#{1}":[115,174],"##SemPy vs. Semantic-Link-Labs":[175,183],"##SemPy vs. Semantic-Link-Labs#{1}":[177,183],"##What It Won’t Do":[184,192],"##What It Won’t Do#{1}":[186,192],"##Practitioner Verdict":[193,205],"##Practitioner Verdict#{1}":[195,205]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Gulab Chand Tejwani","target":"Gulab Chand Tejwani","line":5}],"metadata":{"title":"The Python Library That Reads Your Power BI Models Like Data. Most Fabric Teams Have Never Opened It.","source":"https://medium.com/towards-artificial-intelligence/the-python-library-that-reads-your-power-bi-models-like-data-a8aa1408f2cd","author":["[[Gulab Chand Tejwani]]"],"published":"2026-07-18","created":"2026-07-27","description":"Semantic Link — the SemPy library — ships preinstalled in every Fabric notebook. It can list every measure in your tenant’s models, evaluate them with filters from Python, run DAX programmatically, and validate your data against the relationships your model claims to have. I’ve used it to automate work that used to consume entire client weeks. Here’s the practitioner’s tour, with the code.","Processed":"Unprocessed"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[45,71],[85,99],[117,163]],"key":"projects/The Vault/99.System/InboxArchive/2026-07/The Python Library That Reads Your Power BI Models Like Data. Most Fabric Teams Have Never Opened It.md"},
